BT 1 0 0 1 0 83.2 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 13.2 TL (H is a proposed framework for investigating a system through recursively deeper levels of abstract difference \(AD\). At) Tj T* (each level, an AD represents structure in the behaviour observed at the preceding level. The framework aims to) Tj T* (identify useful mathematical representations or transformations, then use them to reason about a system's) Tj T* (progression. In the initial machine-learning demonstration, a model state at epoch 18 was estimated from earlier) Tj T* (checkpoints at epochs 1 and 10. The resulting predicted model achieved 92.5% accuracy on the original validation set) Tj T* (and 96.0% accuracy on a separate 200-example evaluation set. These results are promising for this one setup, but do) Tj T* (not establish a universal prediction method or prove the general validity of H.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
